{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MAT",
  "chapter": 12,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At that time Jesus went on the sabbath through the corn, and his disciples were hungry, and began to pluck the ears of corn, and to eat.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But when the Pharisees saw it, they said to him, Behold, thy disciples do that which it is not lawful to do on the sabbath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he said to them, Have ye not read what David did when he was hungry, and they that were with him;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How he entered into the house of God, and ate the show-bread, which it was not lawful for him to eat, neither for them who were with him, but only for the priests?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or have ye not read in the law, that on the sabbath the priests in the temple profane the sabbath, and are blameless?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I say to you, that in this place is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " greater than the temple.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if ye had known what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice, ye would not have condemned the guiltless.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the Son of man is Lord even of the sabbath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he had departed thence, he went into their synagogue.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And behold, there was a man who had ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hand withered. And they asked him, saying, Is it lawful to heal on the sabbath? that they might accuse him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to them, What man shall there be among you, that shall have one sheep, and if it shall fall into a pit on the sabbath, will he not lay hold on it, and lift ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How much then is a man better than a sheep? wherefore it is lawful to do well on the sabbath days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then saith he to the man, Stretch out thy hand. And he stretched ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " was restored to a sound state like the other.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the Pharisees went out, and held a council against him, how they might destroy him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But when Jesus knew ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", he withdrew himself from thence: and great multitudes followed him, and he healed them all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And charged them that they should not make him known:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Isaiah the prophet, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, my servant, whom I have chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased: I will put my spirit upon him, and he shall show judgment to the Gentiles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall not contend, nor cry; neither shall any man hear his voice in the streets.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A bruised reed shall he not break, and smoking flax shall he not quench, till he shall send forth judgment to victory.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And in his name shall the Gentiles trust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then was brought to him one possessed with a demon, blind and dumb; and he healed him, so that the blind and dumb both spoke and saw.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all the people were amazed, and said, Is not this the son of David?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But when the Pharisees heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", they said, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doth not cast out demons, but by Beelzebub the prince of the demons.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus knew their thoughts, and said to them, Every kingdom divided against itself, is brought to desolation; and every city or house divided against itself, shall not stand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if Satan casteth out Satan, he is divided against himself; how then shall his kingdom stand?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if I by Beelzebub cast out demons, by whom do your children expel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? therefore they shall be your judges.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if I cast out demons by the Spirit of God, then the kingdom of God is come to you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or else, how can one enter into a strong man's house, and seize his goods, except he shall first bind the strong man? and then he will plunder his house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that is not with me, is against me; and he that gathereth not with me, scattereth abroad.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore I say to you, All manner of sin and blasphemy shall be forgiven to men: but the blasphemy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "against",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Holy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Spirit shall not be forgiven to men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And whoever speaketh a word against the Son of man, it shall be forgiven him: but whoever speaketh against the Holy Spirit, it shall not be forgiven him, neither in this world, neither in the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "world",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Either make the tree good, and its fruit good; or else make the tree corrupt, and its fruit corrupt: for the tree is known by ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "its",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fruit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O generation of vipers, how can ye, being evil, speak good things? for out of the abundance of the heart, the mouth speaketh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A good man, out of the good treasure of the heart, bringeth forth good things: and an evil man, out of the evil treasure, bringeth forth evil things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I say to you, That for every idle word that men shall speak, they shall give account in the day of judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For by thy words thou shalt be justified, and by thy words thou shalt be condemned.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then certain of the scribes and of the Pharisees answered, saying, Master, we would see a sign from thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he answered and said to them, An evil and adulterous generation seeketh for a sign, and there shall no sign be given to it, but the sign of the prophet Jonah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For as Jonah was three days and three nights in the whale's belly: so shall the Son of man be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The men of Nineveh shall rise in judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it: because they repented at the preaching of Jonah; and behold, a greater than Jonah ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " here.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The queen of the south shall rise up in the judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it: for she came from the uttermost parts of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon; and behold, a greater than Solomon ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " here.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the unclean spirit is gone out of a man, he walketh through dry places, seeking rest, and he findeth none.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then he saith, I will return into my house from whence I came out; and when he is come, he findeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " empty, swept, and garnished.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then goeth he, and taketh with himself seven other spirits more wicked than himself, and they enter in and dwell there: and the last ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "state",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of that man is worse than the first. Even so shall it be also to this wicked generation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "While he was yet speaking to the people, behold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mother and his brethren stood without, desiring to speak with him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then one said to him, Behold, thy mother and thy brethren stand without, desiring to speak with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.48",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.48",
      "verse": 48,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he answered and said to him that told him, Who is my mother? and who are my brethren?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.49",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.49",
      "verse": 49,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he stretched forth his hand towards his disciples, and said, Behold my mother and my brethren!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.12.50",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.12.50",
      "verse": 50,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For whoever shall do the will of my Father who is in heaven, the same is my brother, and sister, and mother.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
